>
  <p>Nuvellum publishes reporting, analysis and culture coverage with clear labeling, source discipline and a visual language designed to feel considered rather than disposable.</p>
  <h2>What we publish</h2>
  <p>News reporting, analysis, explainers, opinion, reviews and cultural coverage are treated as distinct formats. The label should tell the reader what kind of work they are entering before the first paragraph does.</p>
  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Published reporting is expected to remain traceable to its sources. Higher-risk material is held to a separate verification step before publication, while corrections are surfaced when a factual change is material.</p>
  <span slot="aside">Nuvellum’s editorial and technical systems are still being built in public. The publication’s standards pages describe the rules the product is expected to enforce.</span>
</InstitutionalPage>
